    {
      "id": "SYqX3yCo1WkiHt3u9ndF2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 126,
      "y": -1761.613636363636,
      "width": 959.1986694335938,
      "height": 980,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#343a40",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1L",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 672089349,
      "version": 1614,
      "versionNonce": 1193885676,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784377060619,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design URL Shortner like Bit.ly\n\ni/p -> https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/system-design/distributed-coordination-services-zookeeper-system-design/\n\no/p -> http://bit.ly/4t7xcj\n\n1. Functional Requirements                                        \n- create a short url from long url                                 \n - custom url(optional)                                   \n - expirationDate(optional)\n- redirect to long url from short url\n\n\n2. Non-Functional Requirements    \n- availabily > consistency (CAP theorem)\n- low latency (redirect url 200ms)\n- shorten url should be unique\n- 1B url\n\n3. Core Entities\n- User\n- short url\n- long url\n\n4. API creation\n - GET /v1/url/{shortUrl}\n  -return long url\n\n- POST /v1/generateLongUrl\n -request body\n    {\n        shorlUrl\n        expirationDate?\n        custom\n\n    }\n\n    with response code 301 or 302 \n    301 --> browser cached data the url so next time redirect will be fast\n    302 --> browser wont cach the data, if mapped will be changed later then this approach is better\n\n- response { longUrl }\n\n5. HLD\n\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design URL Shortner like Bit.ly\n\ni/p -> https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/system-design/distributed-coordination-services-zookeeper-system-design/\n\no/p -> http://bit.ly/4t7xcj\n\n1. Functional Requirements                                        \n- create a short url from long url                                 \n - custom url(optional)                                   \n - expirationDate(optional)\n- redirect to long url from short url\n\n\n2. Non-Functional Requirements    \n- availabily > consistency (CAP theorem)\n- low latency (redirect url 200ms)\n- shorten url should be unique\n- 1B url\n\n3. Core Entities\n- User\n- short url\n- long url\n\n4. API creation\n - GET /v1/url/{shortUrl}\n  -return long url\n\n- POST /v1/generateLongUrl\n -request body\n    {\n        shorlUrl\n        expirationDate?\n        custom\n\n    }\n\n    with response code 301 or 302 \n    301 --> browser cached data the url so next time redirect will be fast\n    302 --> browser wont cach the data, if mapped will be changed later then this approach is better\n\n- response { longUrl }\n\n5. HLD\n\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
